Check on the bounded nature of delta keff variances of each perturbed system
=======================================================================================
This check is based on examining, for each perturbed system, the probability density function
of the absolute value of the (delta keff) obtained for each cycle.
A sufficient condition for the variance of the (delta keff) to be bounded is that the probability density
tends to zero faster than 1 / (delta keff)^3 when (delta keff) tends to +/-infinity.
That is why the asymptotic slope of the probability density function is estimated on a log-log scale.
This slope must be greater than 3 (in absolute value).
